{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"extralegal-durative-beaver","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\nThe `reconcile-check` vocabulary was retired by `mechanical-bitter-basenji`\n(`0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b`, merged as `8e14d667da28`), but one **live state path** still writes it.\nThis is a deliberate, operator-directed carve-out from that story — filed here so it is tracked\ndebt rather than an unexplained residual.\n\n## The residual\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py`\n\n- **`:717`** — the pause **writer** still persists `gated_mode=\"reconcile-check\"`.\n- **`:658`** — the matching **decoder**.\n\nEverything else in the retired family is clean. A whole-tree sweep\n(`grep -rn \"reconcile-check\\|reconcile_check\\|RECONCILE_CHECK\"`) at `12a10f3ab4ef` found\n`.github/`, `Jenkinsfile`, `scripts/` and `src/rebar/schemas/` free of it, and the remaining hits\nare all explained:\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py:57` — the **intentional** narrow decode alias\n  retained by 0cfc's AC3: it maps only the persisted sentinel to `DRY_RUN`, is not an enum member,\n  and is absent from `MODE_CAPS`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py:102-104` — the retirement **rejection message**,\n  which must name the retired vocabulary in order to route users to `preview` / `fsck` / `status`.\n- `docs/adr/0092`, `docs/adr/0099`, `docs/adr/0083` — ADR prose. Historical records of decisions\n  taken when the vocabulary was live; rewriting them would falsify the record.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py:350` — the `\"reconcile_check_error\"` log key. **Unrelated\n  subsystem** (the review-bot's Gerrit vote-reconcile loop). A name collision, not a residual.\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/...` — frozen eval fixtures and corpora.\n\nSo `_ref_lock.py:658/717` is the only genuine live-state survivor.\n\n## Why it was left\n\n0cfc's description carries a \"Final AC2 Option B execution note\" recording that **the operator\nexplicitly directed that pass not to edit** the pause-state decoder/writer at those lines. That is\na description-level carve-out, not a comment-level one, so it was a deliberate scope decision\nrather than an omission. It does mean 0cfc's AC2 (\"no live route/mode/state path retains the\nvocabulary\") cannot be satisfied on a literal reading, which is why that ticket's AC2 now points\nhere.\n\n## Why it is low priority but not zero\n\nThe value is persisted pause state, and the decoder that reads it is present and correct, so\nnothing is broken today. The cost is that a retired name survives in written state: any future\nreader of a pause record sees vocabulary the codebase otherwise says does not exist, and a later\ncleanup that removes the decoder without migrating the writer would strand existing pause records.\nThe two lines must therefore move together.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 The pause **writer** at `_ref_lock.py:717` persists a current-vocabulary value instead of\n      `\"reconcile-check\"`.\n- [ ] AC2 Existing persisted pause records written with the old sentinel are **still readable** —\n      either migrated, or read by a narrowly-retained decoder in the same shape as the one AC3 of\n      0cfc already sanctions in `mode.py:57`. Dropping the decoder in the same change that changes\n      the writer is the failure mode this AC exists to prevent.\n- [ ] AC3 A test writes a pause record with the OLD sentinel and asserts it still decodes correctly\n      after the change, and a second test asserts new writes use the new value. Both directions, so\n      the migration cannot silently break old records.\n- [ ] AC4 The whole-tree sweep for `reconcile-check|reconcile_check|RECONCILE_CHECK` is re-run and\n      its output recorded here, with every surviving hit individually explained (the categories\n      above are the expected survivors: the intentional decode alias, the rejection message, ADR\n      prose, the unrelated review-bot log key, and frozen eval fixtures).\n- [ ] AC5 `0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b`'s AC2 disposition is updated to note the residual is discharged.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (it exits 127,\na silent no-op) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Do not touch the shared main\ncheckout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","id":"d433-782d-e74d-4b27","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler pause state still persists gated_mode=\"reconcile-check\" after the vocabulary was retired"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788658798179781530,"uuid":"02cfaf0c-c6fb-4301-a655-73d55681abda"}